<para>This function sends an IPI request to configure one or more glitch detectors via XLOADER_CMD_ID_CONFIG_GLITCH_DETECTOR. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>    Each word in GdCfgWords packs four u8 fields (LSB first):
    - [7:0]   GD type (XLOADER_GD_TYPE_*)
    - [15:8]  depth
    - [23:16] width
    - [31:24] ref_voltage

    Use XLoader_PackGlitchDetectorCfg() to build each word. Payload length is 1..5
</verbatim></para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the client instance. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>GdCfgWords</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Array of packed glitch-detector config words. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>NumWords</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of config words (XLOADER_GD_CFG_MIN_LEN .. MAX_LEN).</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS on success.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM on invalid arguments.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Error code from PLM on failure. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
